      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11426066::web::012::results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Approximately half of the Cu-site population should be replaced by Pt.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11426066::web::012::results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Arc melting followed by annealing near 900 °C and slow cooling will allow L10 ordering to develop.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "VSM or SQUID magnetometry can be used to measure the magnetic hysteresis and coercivity.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11426066::web::023::experimental_section"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pt modification will form nanoscale L10 precipitates within a predominantly FCC matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The nanoscale ordered L10 regions will provide additional domain-wall pinning sites.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chemical ordering lowers crystal symmetry and enhances intrinsic magnetocrystalline anisotropy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11426066::web::012::results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enhanced magnetocrystalline anisotropy increases the energy barrier for domain-wall motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11426066::web::012::results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stronger domain-wall pinning raises the coercive field.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Pt-modified alloy will show a wider hysteresis loop and higher coercive field than the Pt-free baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11426066::web::012::results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The matched baseline is the original disordered FCC FeCoNiMnCu alloy processed identically but without Pt.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coercivity increase should occur only when processing permits controlled chemical ordering.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11426066::web::012::results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Excessive grain growth may weaken the proposed domain-wall pinning effect.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "An overabundance of the ordered phase may compromise microstructural integrity and weaken pinning.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The magnitude of coercivity improvement will depend on Pt fraction and the volume fraction and spatial distribution of the ordered phase.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
